    "gate_decided": "Matt, 2026-11-25: strict against all three baselines. The margin's mean absolute error must be below home court, last season's ratings and the source's Elo, each with the 90% interval of the difference (resampled by game date) below zero. The edge over the ratings alone is reported, not gated. The gate statistic on the development seasons (cbb/ratings/output/development.json; 2024 and 2025, 11,281 games): against Elo -0.71 points (-0.83 to -0.60), against last season's ratings -1.18 (-1.27 to -1.09), against home court -2.33 (-2.48 to -2.18); each also clear of zero in each season alone. Every candidate gate passed there, so the choice was not made to pass.",
    "secondary": "Reported, not gating (the module's `secondary`): mean absolute error of the total; log loss, accuracy and calibration of the home win probability; margin error by month; and by game type through `segment` (non-conference, conference, conference tournament, national postseason). The closing line's error is an aggregate benchmark on the games that have one: never an input, never per game.",
    "too_good": 8.0,
    "too_good_note": "The closing line's error on the development seasons was 8.8 points. A margin error below 8.0 would mean a leak, not a better model.",
    "not_applicable": {
      "label_permutation": "A rating model: its forecasts for the test season come from that season's own results through the walk-forward, not from labels learned on the training seasons, so shuffling the training seasons' outcomes leaves it predictive. The check that it reads no later game is the scramble test (tests/test_cbb_model.py: forecasts and features for a date do not change when every later game is changed)."
    },
    "known_hindsight": "Seasons before 2026-11-24 come from the source as it stands now, not as it stood then (revision_safe: false). The inputs are final scores, box-score counts and minutes, which are rarely revised. The source's pre-game Elo (a baseline, not an input) is read as stored today.",
    "reproduction": "Deterministic (closed-form ridge and least squares). Official runs happen in CI.",
